        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(scripts): preserve emoji in GitHub API errors",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where operators using `scripts/gh-read` could receive malformed GitHub API error output when a response placed an emoji across the diagnostic character limit.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe error-body reader now reuses the repository's surrogate-safe truncation helper while preserving its existing character cap and `[truncated]` marker. Focused tests cover both split and complete surrogate-pair boundaries.\n\nAI-assisted: yes. I reviewed the external response, reader, stderr sink, and shared helper contract.\n\n## User Impact\n\nGitHub API failures reported by `scripts/gh-read` remain valid Unicode. ASCII output, successful JSON responses, timeouts, and existing size limits are unchanged.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Before: `\"abc\\u{1f600}tail\".slice(0, 4)` ends in lone UTF-16 code unit `0xd83d`.\n- Live read-only request to the versioned GitHub REST API returned the documented JSON error body (`message`, `documentation_url`, and `status`). See https://docs.github.com/en/rest/using-the-rest-api/troubleshooting-the-rest-api?apiVersion=2022-11-28.\n- Added focused coverage in `test/scripts/gh-read.test.ts` for split and complete surrogate-pair boundaries.\n- `git diff --check`\n- `node_modules/.bin/oxfmt --check scripts/gh-read.ts test/scripts/gh-read.test.ts`\n- Exact-head CI run https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29404341287: `check-lint` passed and `test/scripts/gh-read.test.ts` passed 14 tests in `checks-node-compact-small-4`.\n- The run's remaining failures are in untouched current-main surfaces, plus an unrelated hooks CLI timeout flake.\n",
        "branch": "fix/gh-read-error-utf16-safe-20260715",
